{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:e5f922413f2fc6627bc086b30434717b79b28d48e47129c573f4f225ddcfa512","title":"When can light residual angular fields generate significant curvature perturbations and non-Gaussianity at the end of warped brane inflation, and do those conditions actually produce an effect in the explicit Kuperstein-embedding case study?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0005"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e50105d51ef65387e4e82eaf2f653c33b204dc8fd44466599fd4b1a11661f07c","title":"Can higher-derivative kinetic gravity braiding slow axion evolution enough to obtain sufficient inflation and a nearly scale-invariant scalar spectrum with a sub-Planckian decay constant, and which parameters can linear cosmological perturbations determine?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0013"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e5c4ae8d8d48db2abfdc5c70db1906ebb678e7fb6d35b741831d0f9d7378e870","title":"Assuming the weak gravity conjecture and a large tensor signal, which large-field axion inflation models obtainable from higher-dimensional Abelian gauge theories have acceptable gauge couplings, compactification scales and charge assignments?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0016"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e5863986c224a03d3413722f3314da42dac40f4d263a3a7e19478c61c83b2d03","title":"What constraints does absence of a measurable asymptotic time advance impose on an isolated massive spin-2 particle's cubic interactions, and when must new physics enter if those constraints fail?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e54ae8831c77ee327c67f00bd322c3faad1bd4d2bfac3931a27cc7f6f871ed21","title":"Does a solution of source-integrated supergravity equations have a fully localized counterpart with the required orientifold and brane backreaction?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0030"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e582170d707f9542b4e61154e86034ad3c00bff677ae446e44e2d5fa751cb1f3","title":"The model links dark-energy evolution to the Higgs potential through a common exponential factor. A negative past value of the Planck-normalized field φ increases the quartic boundary value without directly changing the other Standard Model interactions in the calculation.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0033"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e514d600b2d1e9b9528fe6ea22b770c9809e215461342208281652be1f72bfe5","title":"Do potential slow-roll obstructions exclude quantum de Sitter vacua, or characterize the tree-level boundary of the string landscape? A separate issue is whether families of solutions can approach arbitrarily weak coupling while retaining de Sitter.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0034"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e56e626ef44dcc55050823524f9569398e75093d21d7ec18fbedbc56fa00d6db","title":"Does a scalar potential change the field-space distance relevant to the appearance of light quantum-gravity states? The proposed answer uses the length of a trajectory lifted to the potential graph.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0034"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e5901dc4c4302d1069a11a3b98729dc4a586bc4ec2766cd02c214f6cc5b20d29","title":"What effective interactions make electroweak theta physically relevant, and what ultraviolet gauge coupling enters the baseline estimate? The paper assumes explicit B+L violation and uses Standard Model running to a reduced-Planck-scale cutoff.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0035"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e565ce73124059d78e42feb212809ed6bbd9894b75224b51d00064015c100fd9","title":"Can different scalar theories produce ultracompact stars that both pass the conjectural filters and remain perturbatively stable? The analyzed rotating examples satisfy the first two properties but fail the stability requirement.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0036"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e57e1d89fc7648522699b0c38404e493146e0b5a1ae4c40e6ca23de1f603b81a","title":"How does axionic motion change the proper excursion associated with a fixed radial approach to infinite distance?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0037"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e53e25c8c30346c8ae5b0bb67ebd834dfd92afb6be83ad640b25ba8c4af1c9e9","title":"An additional brane-sector F-term can raise observable-sector superpartner masses independently of the small Kähler-mediated scale. The same auxiliary expectation also carries vacuum energy, so lowering the mediation scale becomes relevant to the cosmological obstruction.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e5ac3d6d919f32cc4db4fc8d7e675de6a361c611b2edc3455beb1c19a17bb7d3","title":"Which parities define this N=1 IIA model? The visually confirmed antiholomorphic sign reversal leaves three odd (1,1) directions, no even directions, and a three-form pair with A0 even and B^0 odd.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e59966e2a780d074cdfedf192144ac3d89a945343f15ab2340ac6dcf73d719c8","title":"Which higher-curvature gravities have tractable linearized spectra and black holes, how do their corrections affect four-dimensional black-hole thermodynamics, and what CFT information can their AdS solutions reveal?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0048"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e547701099a8451170bf0a59ba0185f0925e04e9a7d2cbb37322675770f274e8","title":"What constraints do cosmic censorship and its proposed WGC modification impose holographically on boundary matter, especially the number of colours Nc, and could these constraints obstruct realistic QCD models?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0055"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e54b4ea467d0a0adffecd42a39ec1229e90e80a25d9a809ba7d5d984296b647e","title":"Can homogeneous barrier-crossing decay of a de Sitter minimum occur quickly enough to avoid the TCC concern raised in Appendix C?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0056"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e5137b7007ef0315283ea5017b1117043f0cf4f5c85775630cf68558f6f92223","title":"This orientifold patch provides a concrete setting in which negative orientifold charge, magnetized brane charge and positive flux charge must balance. Its explicit brane families make the assumptions behind finite-vacua counting accessible to scrutiny.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0057"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e52ab289ace8afc14cde4377f2d1454c1a326fe849767515a4e4050a6edb4b72","title":"How can one elementary charge's mass scaling characterize a tower becoming light at infinite distance?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0059"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e5f64689f445d19950941f981afd219bdbc013f05615460dbd4df4bcd2338f3f","title":"When does eliminating an original heavy field at the action level agree with integrating out entropic perturbations?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0061"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e5bf8b5cb7807a67c7b248daa7c7404d64b6b5b027367c112846d5bf64e65f2e","title":"Do lightening and crossings persist for forms, other moduli directions, and other Calabi–Yau constructions, and can the crossing pattern be predicted?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0063"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e5b0ce20d840b1cbf43dcd51edd4f4e639bbbce251b62f78f36eeee9bfc401c2","title":"How do supersymmetric four-derivative interactions modify minimal gauged supergravity, AdS4 observables and black-hole thermodynamics, and can localization determine their coefficients and predict subleading large-N observables?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0065"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e58081b7361d968f1d90bf17da9e4ddef895263128af5bb0a3921ec5ca6a28d9","title":"Can a cosmological constant switching from negative to positive at late times alleviate cosmological tensions while retaining agreement with CMB and BAO observations, and does Bayesian evidence distinguish this extension from ΛCDM?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0067"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e5dae392e32af1980633105a4ba8d88013b2ef3c57f4dd1f8e2029c79d0f7358","title":"Which weak gravity conjectures are supported by quantum gravity examples, what principles might explain them, and how strongly can they constrain effective theories?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0071"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e58cbc0c02f9ba7cb6c531f9459069e66483b7d44c460a288f92762d104c3f81","title":"Which gravitational instantons describe bubble-of-nothing decays of selected AdS backgrounds, and can a non-supersymmetric massive-IIA AdS4 vacuum possess such a decay channel despite reported perturbative and brane-jet stability?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0073"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e55d5230af5a0bd9c24680341898bda250f223ce31b035a50e754ee87dbab91b","title":"A flat scalar direction can affect cosmological evolution through a field-dependent kinetic coefficient even when it does not enter the potential. The model isolates that mechanism in a homogeneous gravity-plus-fluid setting.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0074"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e580623e54876298225afd9606c98bbe29e807ba983dc3a4cae75fdaa6b080f4","title":"Can exact parity or CP be spontaneously broken consistently with quantum gravity, what protects the resulting domain walls, and what cosmological constraints follow?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0078"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e54978d6bdd989dfc35916fe35bc4de186947084dfdcb0c67ee75e92f89b5091","title":"Can one sgoldstino sector realize observationally acceptable inflection-point inflation, stabilized supersymmetry breaking and a tunable positive vacuum energy, and what parameter tuning and superpartner scales follow?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0080"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e509a4e697930ce2b692227396eeace4adb22be6d6781c7ccbabe2f7925c1539","title":"Can perturbative gravity near two dimensions yield a physical, gauge- and parametrization-independent spectrum of curvature-squared composite operators, and what does its extrapolation suggest about relevant directions in four-dimensional asymptotic safety?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0080"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e5217d6bfd5a06bb7a32126b865514eacd2c783cfccf3c2e79aaa94240038adb","title":"Under what restrictions can charged black holes surrounded by quintessence, with or without a cloud of strings, retain horizons when Q>M? The paper interprets these configurations as compatibility between its black-hole implementation of WGC and weak cosmic censorship.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0083"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e5daf8a51912bae59df4bffba2dbfb120086d0a9bb64dcfc31694b62fd2d88ac","title":"What bulk object represents a boundary topological symmetry operator, and can reconstruction explain its metric dependence and the absence of bulk global symmetries without initially assuming bulk gauging?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0086"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e55aad9de1ad6e454092ea1b9ad28aeda2e9549b5e3ec4c55bb9755356cec568","title":"Does a nonlinear Yang–Mills modification of a charged RN black hole change the scalar-perturbation diagnostic for strong cosmic censorship, and under what charged-scalar conditions can an extremal modified black hole satisfy that diagnostic?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0092"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e5d0e5cca55086c00dcfdb49818eb208aa277167e84a9ff00f7cbb65219184da","title":"Do discrete symmetries arising in heterotic compactifications satisfy anomaly constraints analogous to those for remnants of spontaneously broken gauge symmetries, thereby restricting the light effective theory?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0106"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e5c7adca9df183355afc71a93ae2d64184c52b7a2ad4832d94a3aac770427c98","title":"Can Euclidean de Sitter entropy be understood in string theory as the number of degrees of freedom of a dual quantum mechanics, using the sphere factors of AdS compactifications?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0108"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:e5bdcfcca6b2b3d76471dd555bfe9e180b98edd2f15a902cc53024b206f0ae1b","title":"Can a homogeneous M-theory universe containing supergravity particles and anisotropically wrapped M2-br